      en: "The Senegambia Bridge, also known as the Trans-Gambia Bridge, is The Gambia's most significant modern infrastructure project and a crucial landmark for West African regional integration. Spanning an impressive 1.9 kilometers across the Gambia River near Farafenni, it connects the north and south banks of the country. Its opening in January 2019 marked the end of decades of delays and replaced the often unreliable and time-consuming ferry service that heavily hindered travel and trade between northern and southern Senegal. As a landmark, its high concrete pillars and elegant design dominate the river landscape. The bridge is a symbol of economic revival and political change under President Adama Barrow. It not only facilitates national transport but is also a vital part of the Trans-Gambia Highway, accelerating freight traffic throughout the ECOWAS region. For travelers, the crossing offers an expansive view over the mighty Gambia River and the mangrove forests lining it.",
